id: pm-vcs-phase6stage
title: Stream ordinary large-file staging into native CDC manifests
description: "Connect vcs add to bounded CDC for non-record regular files at least 1 MiB, preserve FileIds across moves and PM attribution, keep status bounded for manifest-backed files, and publish reproducible scale and GC byte receipts."
type: Feature
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T14:41:01.521Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T21:19:12.433Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Native add and status handle large binary files without whole-file buffers; rename plus edit retains FileId and PM change trace; compression-independent identities and range verification pass; GC reports physical candidate and reclaimed bytes; report a 200 MB binary and real tracker copy measurement.
parent: pm-vcs-b7cb
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T14:58:04.824Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: restoring only stageLocked makes native staging streams CDC fail because no binary is staged; restoring only computeStatus fails on the forbidden whole-file reader; restoring only collectGarbage fails the physical-byte receipt assertions. Each mutation was tested in an isolated source copy. Initial 200 MB measurement exposed excessive fsynced loose-object overhead with fine-grained CDC, so ordinary large staging now uses 64 KiB minimum, 1 MiB maximum and an 18-bit Gear mask while existing helper defaults remain unchanged. The partial benchmark scratch copy was removed before remeasurement."
  "2026-10-21T15:14:12.255Z",codex-agent,"Real scale receipt: 200000000 generated binary bytes plus 306 real public tracker files committed natively. Baseline store 201271356 compressed object bytes; after a rename and 2000000-byte middle replacement, store 203550572 (+2279216). Reused 604/611 edited chunks (98.8543%), 98.8683% by bytes. Twenty-one verified warm-cache 4 KiB reads: median 13.6759 ms, p95 52.9613 ms under shared-host load. GC dry-run/apply both 1048920 bytes; both committed generations retained and reachable objects verified. All benchmark data removed. Linked PM test command passed 5/5 with no failures/skips using --timeout 900; the default 120-second attempt timed out. Type checking, lint, duplication (0%) and docstrings pass. Full npm/Bun release gates follow artifact regeneration."
  "2026-10-21T15:46:37.929Z",codex-agent,"CI on both Node 22 and 26 measured 100/100/100/100 coverage but found two regression-fixture failures: the production inventory expected 74 files instead of 75, and the bounded export test accidentally staged a CDC manifest where it intended a legacy 4 MiB blob. Updated the inventory explicitly and construct that legacy blob in the real object store, preserving the exact compressed-size-plus-64-byte strace assertion. The superseded local release run was stopped before retesting; full gates will run again at the corrected head."
  "2026-10-21T15:50:22.583Z",codex-agent,"The corrected legacy-export and production-inventory regressions pass 2/2 both directly and through pm test --run --only-last --progress. Legacy export strace remains one full 4195608-byte serialization/hash pass plus exactly 64 discovery bytes. Linked acceptance metadata now allows 900 seconds under host contention. Full npm/Bun gates at the regenerated corrected head remain pending; CI at the previous head had 1773/1775 passing tests with 100% in every coverage dimension, and is not counted as approval."
  "2026-10-21T16:56:49.045Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed and fixing a reachability data-loss defect under child pm-vcs-phase6tmprefs: a legal tmp-named ref was accepted but omitted by both listing and GC, and apply removed its reachable synthetic payload. Both superseded local validation runs were stopped. Ref publication now uses exclusive randomized reserved-lock names; valid tmp names are traversed and malformed tmp refs fail closed. New regressions cover file and directory roots and a process-shaped publication-name collision."
  "2026-10-21T17:19:45.408Z",codex-agent,"Final 200 MB rerun with the ref repair and a fresh 310-file real tracker copy: baseline store 201282023 bytes; edited 203561239 (+2279216); 604/611 chunks reused (98.8543%), 98.8683% by bytes. Stage plus commit 38265.05 ms baseline and 12080.10 ms edited. Twenty-one warm 4 KiB reads: median 3.9337 ms, p95 26.8466 ms. GC dry/apply both 1048920 bytes, both generations retained, all generated data removed. The pinned SDK 2026.10.15 initialization makes an optional Git rev-parse probe and tolerates ENOENT; initialized native runtime commands passed the strict no-Git test. This SDK gap is reported without an upstream issue or dependency bump."
  "2026-10-21T21:15:52.747Z",codex-agent,"PR 138 review round: remote head is current and contains main. Verified latest review: outside-diff scan incorrectly hashes manifest files as blobs and diffText renders manifest metadata. Fix both with non-Git tracker regressions, executable-mode and fixed-layout coverage, then inspect adjacent consumers for the same defect class. Local checks limited to targeted regressions, typecheck and lint due to host load; CI will run full npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T21:17:17.703Z",codex-agent,"Self-review checked all changed production files and adjacent payload consumers: mergePath already refuses manifest text merging, annotation rejects unsupported kinds, workingContent and fileState reassemble manifests. scan now streams recorded boundaries and preserves executable-mode and symlink semantics; diffText reassembles manifests. Additional diagnostic fixes name linked ref roots too. Existing CI composes the npm release gate but previously only installed Bun; added the unchanged full Bun release gate to both Linux Node matrix jobs."
  "2026-10-21T21:18:33.608Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proofs against the fetched PR head: replacing only Repository.scan makes both native and fixed-layout regressions fail (0/2 pass, whole-file scan materialization); replacing only Repository.diffText makes the content-diff regression fail (0/1 pass, manifest metadata appears instead of the expected removed content line). Test sources import TypeScript directly, so no dist rebuild is needed for these mutations. Each function was restored in finally; the combined targeted regressions pass 7/7 with zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo."
  "2026-10-21T21:19:08.459Z",codex-agent,"PM-linked targeted commands passed: manifest scan/diff 3/3 and GC diagnostics 4/4, all zero failed/skipped/cancelled/todo. Initial authoring check caught an incorrect test-helper import, corrected to engine/instances.ts before these passing runs. No local load timeout occurred. dist is ignored and has no committed files. Full release evidence will come from CI after the self-host archive is refreshed and changes are pushed."
